# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads to the build bucket — not what the image contains.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore *only if* there is no .gcloudignore and the
# directory is a git repo, and the v0.9.3 deploy showed what that actually sent: 667 files and
# 120.7 MiB, of which 333 files were a nested worktree under .claude/ and about 65 MB was
# pitch/video/*.mp4. None of it reaches the image — the Dockerfile COPYs named paths — so it was
# pure upload, on every deploy, of a checkout of this repository inside itself.
#
# The build needs exactly: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/ (the static assets are compiled in
# with include_bytes!), pitch/deck.html, and the runtime files under conformance/ and demo/.
# Everything below is outside that set.

# gcloud excludes .git/ implicitly only while no .gcloudignore exists. Writing one replaces that
# default wholesale, so naming it here is not redundant — leaving it out put 3,722 files of git
# history into the upload, which is the opposite of what this file is for.
.git/

#!include:.gitignore

# A worktree of this repository, nested inside it. target/ is excluded by the include above,
# which is the only reason this was 4.7 GB on disk and not in the upload.
.claude/

# Renders and cuts of the film. The film itself is served from a GCS volume mounted on the
# service, never from the image.
pitch/video/
**/*.mp4

# Prose. Nothing in the build reads it; docs/internal/ is excluded by the include above and must
# stay excluded either way.
docs/

# Local ledgers from a test validator, if one was run in the tree.
test-ledger/
.test-ledger/
